#
# Persist a pasted/uploaded image under the session cwd (<cwd>/.paseo-attachments/) so the
# agent's Read tool can open it by absolute path. The inline base64 vision block is left
# untouched (the model still sees the image); a text block naming the absolute path is
# appended beside it. install.sh applies this idempotently and all-or-nothing via
# patches/image-attachments-persist.mjs — THAT is the applier; this file is the
# human-readable reference / re-derivation copy.
#
# Why: a web-UI image upload reaches the daemon only as inline base64 in
# send_agent_message.images[] — there is no file on disk — and the claude provider merely
# puts it into stream-json as {type:image, source:{base64}}. Nothing exists in the
# filesystem, so Read fails and "look at this screenshot, then edit the file" dead-ends.
# All three materialize paths converge on toSdkUserMessage, so this one function is the
# single edit point.
#
# Three anchors; applied only if all three are present, otherwise skipped whole:

